! printed p.72 lines 9-12, THE MACHINE-CONFIGURATION CLEAR LOOP, on its
! own, over a table whose every byte is distinct.
!
! >>> WHY: A WATCHPOINT CAUGHT THIS LOOP WRITING WORDS IT SHOULD NOT. <<<
! Instrumenting StretchStorage to report every write landing in words
! 1962-1964 of the MCP boot, with the program counter, gave PC
! half-word 4389 = 004222.40 for eight writes.  p.72's checked rows put
! line 11 ("V+C,T COMBO") at 004222.40, and line 10 is the only STORE
! in the loop:
!
!   line  9  004221.00  LX,T TYARA
!   line 10  004221.40  T CM9  CM0000, T MCAD(T IXG)
!   line 11  004222.40  V+C, T COMBO
!   line 12  004223.00  BZXCZ, T CM9
!
! The loop ran exactly eight times -- the right count -- and SIX of the
! eight writes were correct.  Two were not: the writes for the conf
! bytes at field offsets 32 and 128 replaced the whole word with
! unrelated content instead of clearing one byte.
!
! T TYARA carries count 8 and T COMBO value 24 (decoded from the live
! words: 0x01ea8000002007a7 and 0x0000180000001000), so V+C counts down
! and the stride is 24 bits -- three bytes, one row.  T MCAD is
! printed p.63 line 28's SYN(BU,8),0.8, the MACH CONF byte.
!
! EVERY BYTE HERE IS DISTINCT so a stray write names itself: row r is
! (16+r, 32+r, 48+r), and after a correct loop only the middle byte of
! each row -- the conf byte -- is zero.

        SLC, (8)2000.0

START   LX, $8, TABPTR
LOOP    CM0000, MCAD($8)
        V+C, $8, COMBO
        BZXCZ, LOOP
PASS    BEW, $

        CNOP
TABPTR  XW, TABLE, 8, 0
COMBO   XW, 24, 0, 0
        CNOP
TABLE   DD(BU,8), 16, 32, 48
        DD(BU,8), 17, 33, 49
        DD(BU,8), 18, 34, 50
        DD(BU,8), 19, 35, 51
        DD(BU,8), 20, 36, 52
        DD(BU,8), 21, 37, 53
        DD(BU,8), 22, 38, 54
        DD(BU,8), 23, 39, 55

MCAD    SYN(BU,8), 0.8

        END, START
